# web/ — Auditing (audited)

Full guide: `docs/guidelines/web/auditing.md`. Stack: `docs/web-stack.md` §7.

**audited** = change history (`audits` table). Not `bundler-audit` (CVE scan) or read/access logs.

## When to audit

- Tenant domain models: students, guardians, charges, documents, billing plans, etc.
- Include `SchoolAuditable` on models with `belongs_to :school` (`associated_with: :school`).

## Do not audit

- `refresh_tokens`, `webhook_events`, `payments`, `audits`.
- Secrets: `redacted:` / `except:` for passwords, tokens, digests.

## API context

- API base controller includes `AuditContext` — sets `Audited.store[:audited_user]` from `Current.user`.
- Bulk/system work: `Model.without_auditing { ... }`.

## LGPD

- Treat `audits` as sensitive; retention TBD (`docs/open-questions.md`).
- Expose audit history only via Pundit-approved backoffice/school endpoints — not guardians by default.
